{
  "id": "V19",
  "title": "LRFD and Ω₀ forces, support post",
  "intent": "A 2nd-story wall SW-1 sits on two support posts (P-1, P-2) that carry its end forces to the foundation. Checks the LRFD seismic combinations (1.2+0.2S_DS)D + ρE + L and (0.9−0.2S_DS)D + ρE and the Ω₀ ASD / LRFD envelopes (all reported forces only), and that the support post member is sized for max(ASD, Ω₀ ASD) compression (ASCE 7-22 §12.3.3.3) while its base hardware stays ASD.",
  "covers": [
    "ASCE 7-22 §2.3.6 (6), (7)",
    "ASCE 7-22 §2.4.5 with Ω₀",
    "§12.3.3.3 support post",
    "Reported vs design combinations"
  ],
  "handCalc": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "text": "SW-1 (Level 2, 8 ft, h = 10 ft): D = self-weight 10 × 8 × 10/1000 = 0.80 + 100 plf × 8 = 0.80 → D = 1.60 k, R_D = 0.80 k; L = 50 plf × 8 = 0.40 k → R_L = 0.20 k. 1.0E = 3 k → N_E = 3 × 10/8 = 3.750 k. Ω₀ = 2.5 (entered: wood structural panel walls, Table 12.2-1 A.15; Cd 4, Ie 1.0, RC II)."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "text": "ASD (design): T = 0.7 × 3.750 − 0.46 × 0.80 = 2.257 k; C = max[1.14 × 0.80 + 0.7 × 3.750 = 3.537, 1.105 × 0.80 + 0.525 × 3.750 + 0.75 × 0.20 = 3.003] = 3.537 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "text": "LRFD (forces only): C = (1.2+0.2S_DS)D + ρE + L = 1.4 × 0.80 + 3.750 + 0.20 = 5.070 k; T = ρE − (0.9−0.2S_DS)D = 3.750 − 0.7 × 0.80 = 3.190 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "text": "Ω₀ ASD (forces only; support posts): C = 1.14 × 0.80 + 0.7 × 2.5 × 3.750 = 7.474 k (combo (6) with Ω₀ 5.956); T = 1.75 × 3.750 − 0.46 × 0.80 = 6.194 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "text": "Ω₀ LRFD (forces only): C = 1.4 × 0.80 + 2.5 × 3.750 + 0.20 = 10.695 k; T = 2.5 × 3.750 − 0.7 × 0.80 = 8.815 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "text": "SW-1 hardware (ASD, upper story → strap): T = 2.257 k → MSTC40 (3070 lb)."
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "text": "Support post P-1 (Level 1, under the SW-1 left end, on the foundation): it carries the SW-1 end per combination, so its envelopes equal the wall end: ASD T 2.257 / C 3.537 k, LRFD C 5.070 k, Ω₀ ASD C 7.474 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 8,
      "text": "Post base hardware (ASD): T = 2.257 k → HDUE3 (min post (2)2x4). Post member: C_design = max(ASD 3.537, Ω₀ ASD 7.474) = 7.474 k (Ω₀ ASD governs) → (2)2x4 5.00 k < C → (3)2x4 7.50 k. With ASD alone it would be (2)2x4."
    },
    {
      "step": 9,
      "text": "Level 1: SW-2 (10 ft) takes the story shear 5 k; the SW-1 shear reaches it through the diaphragm. Line checks G1–G12 pass."
    },
    {
      "step": 10,
      "text": "SW-1 (Eq. 4.3-1, → governs): v = 1000 × 3.000 / 8 = 375.00 plf, A = 10.5 in², G_a = 16 k/in → 8vh³/(EAb) = 0.0210; vh/(1000G_a) = 0.2344; Δ_HD = 0.097 × 3750.00 / 3070/0.7 = 0.0829 (MSTC40, T = 3750.00 lb); r = 3750.00 / (10.5 × 625) = 0.5714 → Δ_c = 0.0157; h·Δa/b = 10 × (0.0829 + 0.0157) / 8 = 0.1232 → δ = 0.3786 in. Story drift Level 2: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-1 0.3786 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.3786 / 1.0 = 1.515 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 10 × 12 = 2.400 in → OK."
    },
    {
      "step": 11,
      "text": "SW-2 (Eq. 4.3-1, → governs): v = 1000 × 5.000 / 10 = 500.00 plf, A = 10.5 in², G_a = 20 k/in → 8vh³/(EAb) = 0.0224; vh/(1000G_a) = 0.2500; Δ_HD = 0.127 × 5000.00 / 3790 (ASD cap) = 0.1675 (HDUE3, T = 5000.00 lb); r = 5000.00 / (10.5 × 625) = 0.7619 → Δ_c = 0.0224; h·Δa/b = 10 × (0.1675 + 0.0224) / 10 = 0.1899 → δ = 0.4623 in. MSTC40 δ basis = cap/0.7 (strap); HDUE3 basis = ASD cap. Story drift Level 1: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-2 0.4623 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.4623 / 1.0 = 1.849 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 10 × 12 = 2.400 in → OK."
    }
  ],
